"57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-18285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/state.json" "file_sha256" "57a66f06ae49fb4197fc7dd298e5421c480bad9165b1e0e48371e7a5def4cfbf" "basis" 1017 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13990722/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $1.$ Find the value of $k.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f90ed32d06641710e2d2ca7b996069a0ece3a9348e3bc6d82247d75ebaea841c" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c23