ion" "q-73542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f90ed32d06641710e2d2ca7b996069a0ece3a9348e3bc6d82247d75ebaea841c" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/state.json" "file_sha256" "6bdb35a4a91916c18bd3d9d00fa5be36c237dafd79d5fe92bc622d7d61b6eb23" "basis" 1131 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14008121/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer