value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ k & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-2-0)+(-2k-0)+0 \\\\  & =-2k-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(1-(-3)) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-2k-2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{32}^{′}=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k+1} & =1 \\\\ 2 & =k+1 \\\\ k & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f02808fa1a224daf5c03eba5b95b8f15f20aefc040642ac73262147503dde345"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-73542" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-275757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in the inverse of the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nequals $-1.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=${{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-275757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k & -2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ k & -2\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2+k)-(-4+2)-(2k+2) \\\\  & =2+k+2-2k-2 \\\\  & =2-k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{13}^{t}={c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1-1 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{13}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2-k}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{k-2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since we are told that ${a}_{13}^{′}=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{k-2} & =-1 \\\\ -1\\cdot (k-2) & =2 \\\\ k-2 & =-2 \\\\ k & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-275757" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f02808fa1a224daf5c03eba5b95b8f15f20aefc040642ac73262147503dde345"} {"question" "q-275757" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-275757" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{32}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-3-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{32}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{32}^{t}={c}_{23}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{23} & =(-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(2-0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{32}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{32}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{23} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319409" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f02808fa1a224daf5c03eba5b95b8f15f20aefc040642ac73262147503dde345"} {"question" "q-319409" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319409" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n${a}_{12}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find the determinant of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A)=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =2|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|-0|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(6-0)-0(-2-0)-1(1-0) \\\\  & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSince we want the entry ${a}_{12}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}^{t}={c}_{21}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{21} & =(-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(0+1) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{12}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\text{det}(A)}{c}_{21} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{11}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f02808fa1a224daf5c03eba5b95b8f15f20aefc040642ac73262147503dde345"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"} {"question" "q-319413" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{11}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14043807/state.json" "file_sha256" "ec610459965fd20a5bc67726da59b1996f3cc8b91a9e9ba6d070dd4a40981287"}] "usage" {"q-319413" [] "q-73542" [] "q-18285" []} "basis" 1629 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186283598 17592186283599 17592186283600 17592186283601 17592186283602 17592186288564 17592186288567 17592186288568 17592186288569 17592186288570 17592186288571] "immutable_fields" [[17592186283597 :answer-field/correct] [17592186283597 :answer-field/id] [17592186283597 :answer-field/key] [17592186283597 :answer-field/type] [17592186288563 :answer-field/correct] [17592186288563 :answer-field/id] [17592186288563 :answer-field/key] [17592186288563 :answer-field/type] [1759218